d_terminal -- Digital UART Terminal with PTY
==============================================

d_terminal is an XSPICE digital code model providing an interactive serial
terminal via a pseudo-terminal (PTY). It implements a full UART frame with
configurable baud rate, data bits, parity, and stop bits.

Port order: d_in d_out
  d_in  = UART RX input (receives from circuit)
  d_out = UART TX output (sends to circuit)

Parameters:
  baud      - baud rate (default 9600)
  data_bits - data bits 5-9 (default 8)
  parity    - "none", "even", or "odd" (default "none")
  stop_bits - 1 or 2 (default 1)
  pty       - PTY symlink path (e.g. "/tmp/tty")
              Creates /dev/pts/N and a symlink at the given path.
              Write to the PTY slave to inject bytes into the circuit.
              Bytes received from the circuit are written to the PTY.

Examples
--------

1. Simple loopback (TX -> RX on the same node, no PTY):

   .model term d_terminal(baud=9600)
   A1 loop_node loop_node term
   .tran 1u 5m uic

2. Full-duplex cross-connect with two terminals and PTY:

   .model term_a d_terminal(baud=115200 pty="/tmp/tty_a")
   .model term_b d_terminal(baud=115200 pty="/tmp/tty_b")
   A1 rx_a tx_b term_a
   A2 rx_b tx_a term_b

3. With dac_bridge probe for visualization:

   .model term d_terminal(baud=9600 pty="/tmp/tty")
   .model bridge dac_bridge(out_low=0 out_high=5)
   A1 rx tx term
   A_dac [tx] [tx_an 0] bridge
   R_load tx_an 0 10k
   .tran 1u 5m uic
   .control
     write /tmp/output.raw v(tx_an)
   .endc

Files
-----
d_terminal_loopback.cir    -- TX->RX loopback with dac_bridge probe
d_terminal_crosstalk.cir   -- Two-terminal cross-connect (full duplex)
